>> title: Beef Chow Fun
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: beef, rice noodles, chinese, wok, dry-fried
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: gon chow ngau ho, gan chao niu he, 乾炒牛河, dry fried beef ho fun, beef ho fun, beef chow fun
>> servings: 2
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: toss the beef in cornstarch and soda, rest 20 min
>> step.2: stir the sauce, no cornstarch in it
>> step.3: sear the beef 1 min, lift it out
>> step.4: char the noodles 3 min, still between turns
>> step.5: toss it together 1 min, and get it onto the plate

Toss @flank steak{8%oz}(225 g; sliced thin across the grain) with @light soy sauce{2%tsp}, @Shaoxing wine{1%tsp}, @cornstarch{2%tsp}, @baking soda{1/8%tsp}, @water{1%Tbs} and @peanut oil{1%tsp}, and leave it to ~rest{20%min}.

Stir @dark soy sauce{2%tsp}, @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @oyster sauce{2%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp} and @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp} together in a bowl.

Sear @&(~2)beef{} in @peanut oil{1%Tbs} in a #wok{} over the fiercest heat you have for ~stirfry{1%min}, then lift it out while the middle is still pink.

Char @fresh wide rice noodles{12%oz}(340 g; ho fun, at room temperature and pulled apart by hand) in @&(~1)wok{} with @peanut oil{1%Tbs} for ~stirfry{3%min}, pressing them flat and leaving them alone between turns.

Toss @&(~1)noodles{} with @&(~3)sauce{}, @bean sprouts{2%cups}(150 g), @scallions{3}(cut in 2-in lengths) and @yellow chives{1%oz}(30 g; in 2-in lengths) for ~stirfry{1%min}, and get it onto the plate — the sprouts should still be raw in the middle.
